// The harness's fixed code, and the order its generated parts follow in.
//
// Every case runs in a process of its own. A case that traps, crashes, runs
// out of memory or corrupts module state takes no other case with it, and the
// flat-store addresses a case sees are the ones it would see alone -- they do
// not depend on what the cases before it allocated. The parent forks once per
// case rather than being re-run per case by the driver: one binary, one exec,
// and nothing in the parent has allocated before the fork.
//
// Each case's process gets IDTC_SECONDS of wall time -- or its own `timeout N`
// seconds, idtc_secs[k] (judge/more/row.id) -- and IDTC_MEMORY of address
// space. A case that exceeds either, traps or is killed is reported as
// that case failing, at its own file and line.

emit_test_tail() {
  emit_tc_run();
  emit_tc_helpers();
  emit_tc_rest();
} return void;
